# Seaproof

Seaproof lets testers report bugs (with a screenshot and the app's logs) and end users send
feedback and ideas from inside the app. Docs for agents: https://seaproof.io/llms.txt

## Adding it

1. Find the stack and follow its guide exactly:
   - React (Vite and similar): https://seaproof.io/docs/react.md
   - Next.js: https://seaproof.io/docs/nextjs.md
   - Flutter: https://seaproof.io/docs/flutter.md
2. A project and a **test** API key come from https://app.seaproof.io, or from the Seaproof MCP
   server (`https://api.seaproof.io/mcp`, tools `create_project` and `create_api_key`) when it
   is connected with the setup permission. For a web app, add the dev origin as an allowed
   website on the key.
3. Keep the key out of source control: `VITE_SEAPROOF_KEY` or `NEXT_PUBLIC_SEAPROOF_KEY` in
   `.env.local`, or `--dart-define=SEAPROOF_KEY=...` in Flutter. Check the file is git-ignored.
4. Pass the build's commit (`commit` option, or `--dart-define=SEAPROOF_COMMIT`) so reports
   point at the code.
5. Mark personal data: `data-seaproof-mask` on web elements, `SeaproofMask` in Flutter.

## Rules

- Never hard-code an API key; never commit one.
- Test and staging keys show the tester button and attach diagnostics; production keys do
  neither, so production apps open the widget from their own button
  (`useSeaproof().open()` or `SeaproofFeedbackButton`).
- A failing request logs an error code with a fix; look it up at
  https://seaproof.io/docs/errors.md instead of guessing.
